  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "The corridor – drop pass and shot",
  "description": "A row of cones splits the rink lengthways into two corridors. In one, a line (A) stands by the net with all the pucks and a line (B) at the other end. A skates with the puck to the middle of the rink and leaves it for B, who is coming the other way. B takes the puck back towards the net and shoots. A joins the back of line B, and B joins line A.\n\nUse the other corridor for two more lines (C and D) at the same time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Leave the puck dead still at the handover – no little pushes forward."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The receiver arrives at speed and takes the puck straight on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "High tempo in the skating."
    }
  ],
